        - _Inflammatory Balance_: Omega -6 and omega -3 fatty acids are precursors to molecules that regulate inflammation. While omega -6 fatty acids are generally pro-inflammatory, omega -3 fatty acids have anti-inflammatory effects. An imbalance with a high proportion of omega -6 to omega -3 can lead to chronic low-grade inflammation, which is associated with various chronic diseases.
